  portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 828491a09d5d2d242a9344ac7a58b638, type: 3}
  journalLore: 'Every waterfall has one, the old folk say: a grey man sitting in the spray with a fiddle, playing a tune that makes the trees dance. Bring him a fat ram and he will teach you to play. Bring him nothing and you will hear the tune anyway, and follow it into the water.'
  journalAdvice: 'It keeps away and flings the cold spray of the falls, and its tune stirs the creatures near it. It is all bone and wet hair: close in and it breaks easily.'
  journalHabitat: Waterfalls, rivers and still meres
  journalKillsToKnow: 3
